{"Env variable naming mismatch breaks webhook authentication - .env.example documents CALCOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET and CALCOM_WEBHOOK_HEADER_NAME, but the actual constants file and webhook handler use CALCOM_CREDENTIAL_SYNC_SECRET and CALCOM_CREDENTIAL_SYNC_HEADER_NAME": 0.01411862950772047, "Webhook request body schema mismatches example app payload - webhook schema expects `keys` and `userId` in request body, but example app sends `encryptedKey` and passes `userId` only as query parameter, and targets non-existent path `/api/v1/credential-sync` instead of `/api/webhook/app-credential`": 0.027253497391939163, "Race condition in concurrent OAuth token refresh when credential syncing is enabled - getTokenObjectOrFetch() has no locking mechanism when multiple concurrent requests check token expiry and initiate refresh simultaneously, causing duplicate API calls, potential rate limit violations, and data consistency issues": 0.09288908541202545, "parseRefreshTokenResponse returns raw data instead of parsed result with success flag - function now returns refreshTokenResponse.data instead of full zod parse result, breaking callers that expect .success property and potentially returning incomplete data without callers knowing": 0.03804800659418106, "Missing error handling for credential sync endpoint HTTP errors - function fetches from credential sync endpoint and returns response without checking .ok or status code, causing cryptic failures when endpoint returns 4xx/5xx status": 0.8485405445098877}